//? Title: Cohen’s d and Hedges’ g with noncentral t intervals
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en

> Choose the standard deviation for the design

In the one-sample example, the reference mean is 15 and the standardizer
is the sample SD. The paired example forms a difference for each matched
row and uses the SD of those differences. The independent-groups
example pools its two sample variances by their residual degrees of freedom.

Cohen’s d divides the mean contrast by the chosen SD. Hedges’ g applies
a small-sample bias correction. Both estimates target the population
contrast standardized by its population SD. The interval comes from
inverting the two tails of the noncentral t distribution for that target.

```{cpp, id=standardized-mean-differences, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <datamunge/stats/standardized_effects.hpp>
#include <print>

int main() {
    using namespace datamunge::stats;
    const auto single = one_sample_standardized_mean_difference({13, 17, 21, 19, 16, 22}, 15);
    const auto paired = paired_standardized_mean_difference({10, 13, 11, 16, 14}, {9, 11, 8, 14, 13});
    const auto pooled = pooled_standardized_mean_difference({13, 17, 21, 19, 16, 22}, {11, 16, 17, 15, 12});
    std::println("| Standardization | Observed SD | Cohen’s d | Hedges’ g | 95% interval |");
    std::println("| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- |");
    const auto show = [](const char* label, const StandardizedMeanDifference& fit) {
        const auto [lower, upper] = fit.confidence_interval;
        std::println("| {} | {:.3f} | {:.3f} | {:.3f} | [{:.3f}, {:.3f}] |",
                     label, fit.standardizer, fit.cohen_d, *fit.hedges_g, lower, upper);
    };
    show("One-sample SD", single);
    show("Paired-difference SD", paired);
    show("Pooled independent-sample SD", pooled);
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
| Standardization | Observed SD | Cohen’s d | Hedges’ g | 95% interval |
| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- |
| One-sample SD | 3.347 | 0.896 | 0.754 | [-0.098, 1.833] |
| Paired-difference SD | 0.837 | 2.151 | 1.717 | [0.451, 3.806] |
| Pooled independent-sample SD | 3.033 | 1.253 | 1.145 | [-0.092, 2.542] |
// result_end

